===Etymology===
A [[borrowing]], via other European languages, probably originally from {{etyl|es|lv}} or {{etyl|ca|lv}} {{term|Andorra|lang=es}}, a word of disputed origin. The most probable hypothesis is that it comes from {{etyl|eu|lv}} {{term|andurrial||shrub-covered land|lang=eu}}, but it is also possible that the source is {{etyl|ar|lv}} {{term|الدرا||the forest|lang=ar}} or {{etyl|es|-}} {{term|andar||to walk|lang=es}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{rfap|lang=lv}}

===Proper noun===
{{lv-proper noun|f|4th}}

# [[Andorra]] {{gloss|[[small]] [[country]] in [[Western Europe]], [[between]] [[France]] and [[Spain]], with [[Andorra la Vella]] as its [[capital]]}}
#: '''''Andoras''' karogs'' — the flag of '''Andorra'''
#: '''''Luksemburgas''' premjerministers'' — the prime minister of '''Luxembourg'''
#: ''administratīvi '''Luksemburga''' iedalās trīs distriktos'' — administratively, '''Luxembourg''' is divided into three districts

